On May 9, 1:56 pm, Kogut <bulwersa...@gmail.com> wrote:
> console - display is garbled, probably due to encoding used
> in console for polish edition of win7

Did you try turning off the various graphics options (set both
DECgraphics and IBMgraphics to false) and using solely printable
ASCII characters?  Those should display correctly no matter WHAT
encoding your OS uses (well, unless you take an oversized flatbed
truck to the retrocomputing museum and fetch an ancient EBCDIC-
based system from the days of blinkenlights and punched cards).

I haven't used UnNetHack myself, nor have I ever used a
Polish-localized version of Windows, but I am pretty sure
that all European Windows localizations leave the printable
ASCII characters pretty well alone, placing the L10N- specific
characters in slot 128 and higher (which is exactly where the
American builds put the framing characters and whatnot that
IBMGraphics uses, so it's not surprising that a localized
OS would not be able to display them).

I suppose it might be possible to get DECgraphics to work
under a localized OS by using a terminal emulator that can
be configured to pretend it's a VT100, but I've not tried it.

Going forward, NitroHack and NetHack4 use Unicode;
hopefully other variants will eventually do likewise.


